\f0\fs24 \cf0 1. Go to the \'84Glycan Reader & Modeller\'93 section\
2. Upload respective .pdb file for the glycan type you want to construct and click \'84next\'93\
3. Just confirm the \'84model/chain selection option\'93 the first residue should be 1 and the last 3. Click \'84next\'93\
4. Keep system pH at 7.0, convert the \'84terminal group patching\'93 to \'84first = NNEU\'93 and \'84last=CNEU\'93 to keep the N and C terminus neutral, check the box \'84glycosylation\'93 and add and edit the desired glycan to the respective amino acid, after you are done with that click \'84next\'93\
5. Keep edge distance to 10 and add 0.15 M of NaCl and make the system neutral. Click \'84next\'93\
6. Just click \'84next\'93 on the next page with PME FFT generation\
7. Select the CHARMM36m FF and GROMACS as MD engine. Setting of T and ensemble selection is arbitrary because customised .mdp files are used with correct settings\
\
Regarding glycan building: The linkage to the protein should be kept to \'84beta\'93. Please add the monosaccharides in an ordered fashion. Start by adding the core and then first building the branch with the highest linkage number (e.g. 1-6) first until its very terminus. When that one is finished, go back to the junction and start building the branch with the second highest linkage number (e.g. 1-3). When there are some side-branches on one branch, also always build the one with the highest linkage number first. \
Check out the glyconformer string in Grothaus et al. 2022 in JCIM. It is described their in detail and follows the same concept. }